  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Trip TRP-05063 is an on-demand booking with no scheduled time, so POL-NS-21 runs the 300-second free wait from the driver's arrival: the driver arrived at 18:36:50 and cancelled at 18:43:20, 390 seconds later, 90 seconds beyond the free wait, so the no-show cancellation was validly made on the trip's own timings.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05063"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-21"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.free_wait",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The 18:36:50 auto-arrival that starts the free wait is corroborated on the driver-device trace, whose nearest fix is 3.283 m from the pickup with a reported accuracy of 5 m, inside POL-NS-21's 50 m arrival radius for a STANDARD pickup, and whose intervals never exceed 30 s, so arrival rests on the GPS evidence and not on the trip record alone.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-05063", "EV-TRIP-05063"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-21"],
      "relies_on": "gps_trace.derived.v7.arrival_check",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The payments ledger carries exactly one cancellation-fee line of 5.00 SGD and records the charge as matching the policy fee, so POL-NS-22 applies at its stated amount with no amount adjustment, and the driver is owed DRIVER_COMPENSATION of 5.00 SGD, amount_sgd and driver_compensation_sgd both 5.00.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-05063"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-22", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.derived.money",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-23's message element is satisfied: the driver sent two in-app messages before cancelling (18:37:10, \"Hi I'm downstairs at Blk 5\", and 18:41:30, \"Still waiting ah\") and the chat log shows both were read by the rider (18:37:56 and 18:42:11), the second less than two minutes before the cancellation.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-05063", "EV-TRIP-05063"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-23"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.contact_before_cancel.messages",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The no-show is admitted on the rider's own side: her counter-statement says she asked for five more minutes because she was finishing a work call, which places her away from the pickup when the free wait expired at 18:41:50, and the trip record's RIDER_NO_SHOW reason code is consistent with it; the driver waited the full period and the fee was earned on this trip's facts.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05063", "EV-CHAT-05063"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-21", "POL-NS-22"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.cancellation_reason_code",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-23's call element is the one element the driver cannot put up, and the driver states that plainly: in_app_calls carries a single 35-second answered call at 18:38:40 and the record attributes it to the rider, and the pre-pass derivation records call_count 0 and obligation_met false, so the driver does not assert a driver-placed call and does not ask the Tribunal to read the element away; the driver submits only that the parties were in live in-app voice contact during the free wait on the rider's own account, and that nothing else in the record displaces the fee earned under POL-NS-21 and POL-NS-22.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05063", "EV-CHAT-05063"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-23"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.contact_before_cancel.call_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Every artifact the driver relies on is COMPLETE at weight 1.0, so POL-GEN-02 sets no confidence ceiling on these facts, and at a contested value of 5.00 SGD POL-GEN-22 places the dispute below the 10.00 SGD band where POL-NS-26 makes the no-show ruling final; the case should be decided on its merits rather than referred.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05063", "EV-GPS-05063", "EV-CHAT-05063", "EV-FARE-05063"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-02", "POL-GEN-22", "POL-NS-26"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "NO_ACTION",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "This is the driver's filing against a refund the platform has already issued: the 5.00 SGD no-show fee was refunded to the rider and withheld from the driver (EV-FARE-05063: refund_issued_sgd 5.00, total_charged 5.00; EV-TRIP-05063: fee_reversed at 2026-09-04T22:55:20). The driver's claim to that 5.00 SGD fails, so nothing moves and the present state stands.\n\nWhy the fee does not stand: POL-NS-23 requires, before a driver cancels for no-show, BOTH (a) at least one in-app chat message from the driver to the rider, and (b) at least one in-app call placed BY the driver to the rider, each before the 18:43:20 cancellation. The message limb is met: MSG-05063-001 at 18:37:10 and MSG-05063-002 at 18:41:30 (EV-CHAT-05063), both read by the rider. The call limb is not met: EV-TRIP-05063 carries exactly one in-app call, placed_by the RIDER at 18:38:40 for 35 s, and its derived contact check records call_count 0, calls [] and obligation_met false; EV-CHAT-05063 contains two text messages and no voice-call entry. A call the rider placed cannot discharge the driver's obligation, so the driver's account that he 'called the passenger' is not supported by the record. Under POL-NS-23 one missing element voids the fee and the rider is not charged, with no driver compensation.\n\nWhat is accepted on the driver's side: this is an on-demand trip with no scheduled time, so under POL-NS-21 the 300 s free wait ran from the driver's arrival at 18:36:50 and expired at 18:41:50; the cancellation at 18:43:20 came 390 s after arrival, 90 s beyond the wait. The arrival is corroborated by the GPS trace (nearest fix 3.283 m from the pickup, reported accuracy 5 m, inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius — EV-GPS-05063), and the ledger charged exactly the POL-NS-22 fee of 5.00 SGD. Those points are correct, but they do not decide the fee: POL-NS-23's contact condition is a separate gate, and it failed. The rider's concession that she asked for five more minutes is consistent with the timings and is treated as evidence, but it likewise does not cure the missing driver call.\n\nTo the rider: the 5.00 SGD stays with you, exactly as the platform already placed it, and you are not charged again.\n\nTo the driver: your claim to keep the fee is not supported; the 5.00 SGD already recovered from you is not returned, because the trip record shows you did not place the required in-app call before cancelling.\n\nNo referral attaches: the fee charged is the policy 5.00 SGD, so POL-NS-22's amount check adds nothing; POL-NS-24's goodwill credit does not arise (you did arrive and did message, so there was no failure to attempt contact); and the rider's no_show_cancellations_30d is 0, so POL-NS-25's repeat flag does not fire. The missing traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-05063-01 (weight 0.0) carries no fact any no-show clause needs and raises no open question. The artifacts carrying the deciding facts (EV-TRIP-05063, EV-CHAT-05063, EV-FARE-05063) are COMPLETE at weight 1.0, so no confidence ceiling applies, and at a contested value of 5.00 SGD below the 10.00 SGD band POL-NS-26 makes this ruling final."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

