    "explanation": "To the driver: you filed to keep the 5.00 SGD no-show fee after the platform refunded it to the rider and recovered it from you. The timing is with you. This was an on-demand booking with no scheduled time, so under POL-NS-21 the 300-second free wait ran from your arrival at the pickup at 18:36:50 (EV-TRIP-05063, corroborated by a GPS fix 3.28 m from the pickup at 5 m reported accuracy, EV-GPS-05063) and expired at 18:41:50; you cancelled at 18:43:20, 390 seconds after arriving, 90 seconds past the free wait. But POL-NS-23 puts a separate condition on charging a no-show fee: before cancelling you must have sent at least one in-app message AND placed at least one in-app call to the rider, both before cancellation. You sent two messages (18:37:10 and 18:41:30, EV-CHAT-05063), so the message limb is met. The call limb is not. EV-TRIP-05063's in-app call record contains exactly one call, placed by the rider at 18:38:40 for 35 seconds; the record's own contact check records call_count 0 and obligation_met false, and EV-CHAT-05063 holds no voice-call entry either. A call the rider placed does not discharge your obligation, and your own submissions concede this limb cannot be put up. Under POL-NS-23 the 5.00 SGD fee is therefore voided and you receive no compensation. To the rider: the 5.00 SGD stays refunded to you. POL-NS-23 voids the fee, so you are not charged; EV-FARE-05063 already records payment_status REFUNDED with refund_issued_sgd 5.00 and total_charged 5.00, and the fee_reversed event at 2026-09-04T22:55:20 confirms the 5.00 SGD went back to you and was withheld from the driver. Because the driver is the filing party and his claim fails, POL-GEN-03 is read from the present state: NO_ACTION, with amount_sgd and driver_compensation_sgd both null. Nothing further is collected from you and nothing is returned to the driver. No referral attaches. The fee charged is exactly the 5.00 SGD POL-NS-22 fixes, so the POL-NS-22 fee-amount referral does not arise; the driver did attempt contact, so POL-NS-24's goodwill credit does not arise; and the rider profile's no_show_cancellations_30d is 0, below POL-NS-25's threshold of 3, so no repeat-no-show referral arises. The missing traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-05063-01, weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT) carries no fact any no-show clause needs, so it raises no POL-GEN-26 open question. Confidence rests on the COMPLETE weight-1.0 trip record and chat log that carry the deciding fact, and the contested value of 5.00 SGD is below 10.00 SGD, where POL-GEN-22 and POL-NS-26 make the ruling final."
