    "explanation": "To both parties: the fee of 5.00 SGD does not stand, so nothing moves back to the driver and the money the rider has already received stays with her. Here is why.\n\nThe trip timings are not in dispute and the driver's account of them is correct. This was an on-demand booking, so under POL-NS-21 the 300-second free wait runs from arrival: the driver arrived at Block 5, Holland Close at 18:36:50 (recorded arrival corroborated by the driver-device trace EV-GPS-05063, whose nearest fix is 3.28 m from the pickup with a reported accuracy of 5 m, inside the 50 m arrival radius for a STANDARD pickup), the free wait expired at 18:41:50, and the driver cancelled at 18:43:20 — 390 seconds after arrival, 90 seconds beyond the free wait (EV-TRIP-05063). The rider's own statement that she asked for five more minutes because she was finishing a work call confirms she was not at the pickup when the wait expired, and the RIDER_NO_SHOW reason code is consistent with that. The driver's free-wait and arrival points (POL-NS-21, EV-TRIP-05063, EV-GPS-05063) are therefore accepted.\n\nThose points are not enough, because POL-NS-23 makes a no-show fee conditional on a separate contact obligation: before cancelling, the driver must have both sent at least one in-app message AND placed at least one in-app call to the rider, both before cancelled_at. The message element is met — the driver messaged at 18:37:10 and 18:41:30 (EV-CHAT-05063, both read by the rider). The call element is not. The only in-app call on this trip is the one placed BY THE RIDER at 18:38:40 and answered for 35 seconds (EV-TRIP-05063, in_app_calls, placed_by RIDER); the trip record's own derived check records call_count 0 and obligation_met false, and the chat log (EV-CHAT-05063) contains two text messages and no voice-call entry. The driver's submission does not assert a driver-placed call — it concedes it cannot — and relies instead on the parties having been in live voice contact during the wait on the rider's account. That is correct as far as it goes, but POL-NS-23 requires the call to have been placed by the driver to the rider, and a call the rider placed does not discharge that obligation. So the driver's claims for DRIVER_COMPENSATION of 5.00 SGD under POL-NS-22 are rejected, and the fee is voided under POL-NS-23: the rider is not charged, with no driver compensation.\n\nOn the money: EV-FARE-05063 records the 5.00 SGD fee as already refunded (payment_status REFUNDED, refund_issued_sgd 5.00), and EV-TRIP-05063 records the fee_reversed event at 2026-09-04T22:55:20, refunded to the rider and withheld from the driver. The rider has therefore already received the 5.00 SGD she is owed. Because the driver is the filing party and his claim fails, the present state stands: the ruling is NO_ACTION, with amount_sgd and driver_compensation_sgd both null, so no further money moves and the disputed charge is not restored against the rider.\n\nNo referral attaches. POL-NS-25's repeat no-show flag operates only at 3 or more no-shows counting this trip if the fee stands; the rider's rider_profile.no_show_cancellations_30d is 0 and the fee does not stand, so it does not fire. POL-NS-22's fee-amount check does not fire, because the ledger charged exactly the policy fee of 5.00 SGD. POL-NS-24's goodwill credit does not fire either: the driver did arrive and did attempt contact, so the driver-no-show condition is absent. The missing traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-05063-01 (weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT) carries no fact, and no no-show element this ruling needs — the driver's messages, the calls, the cancellation time and the arrival — depends on it, so its absence raises no POL-GEN-26 open question. All of the facts this ruling rests on come from COMPLETE artifacts at weight 1.0 (EV-TRIP-05063, EV-CHAT-05063), the contested value of 5.00 SGD sits below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD band, and POL-NS-26 makes the ruling final at that value, so no escalation is warranted."
